    {
      "name": "search_providers",
      "description": "Search licensed behavioral health providers by US state, insurance, care type, clinical needs, availability windows, language, and other matching filters. Use this when the user wants to find therapists or medication-management clinicians. Required input is a US state and insurance. Use self_pay when the customer is uninsured. Timezone is inferred from the state when omitted. Defaults are individual therapy and virtual care, searching all upcoming availability (at most 6 slots per provider, 4 providers per page). Virtual matches are statewide: a provider licensed in the requested state can serve the customer elsewhere in that state. For in-person searches only, optional preferredLocation (latitude/longitude) and radiusMiles must be provided together to limit results to nearby clinics. ZIP and city are valid in-person origins: convert a US ZIP centroid or city center to latitude/longitude, and send originZip when a ZIP was used. Do not tell the customer ZIP is unsupported. siteOfCare is VIRTUAL by default, IN_PERSON when asked, or EITHER when the customer chose Either. Pass desiredDate, daysOfWeek, and hourRanges only when the customer named a schedule. Classify every stated criterion in constraints as MUST_HAVE or PREFERENCE. Must-haves stay hard filters; ask before relaxing any of them, then keep the original value and set relaxed=true. Preferences on insurance, gender, availability, populations, and geo are omitted from the hard filter. This search does not filter by budget. The tool is read-only and does not book appointments, cancel care, or change provider data. Results include provider profile fields and that provider's own matching openings. resultCount is the number of provider cards on this page. Empty results mean no matching providers were found. When the first search in a turn returns no providers, the conversation response must include a Continue on WiseMatch link on its own line to https://app.wisematch.com/wisematch/start so it opens the WiseMatch Guided Flow in a new browser tab, even if a later search in that turn returns providers. Do not link any other WiseMatch page. This tool does not render the widget. After the final search in a turn, including any relaxed follow-up searches, call render_provider_results with this result's searchId. Pass providerIds only to show a subset of those providers",
